# The Python environment. Rebuilt by install.sh; never committed.
.venv/
# Downloaded wheels for an offline install (docs/01 §7). About 60 MB,
# architecture-specific, and rebuilt in one command.
wheels/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# PlatformIO's build tree. 38 MB of objects rebuilt from source in a minute.
firmware/Firmware/.pio/

# The duplicate image verify.sh leaves behind. Byte-identical to the course
# binary under a different name, and having two candidates on the morning of
# the workshop is how the wrong one gets flashed.
firmware/binaries/flatsat-firmware-v1.0.5-norf.uf2

# Captures and dumps produced while working. The flash dump from lab 2.9 has
# the AES key in it.
captures/
*.pcap
*.bin
!firmware/binaries/*.uf2
# The challenge material is the course, not a working file. It ships.
!challenges/*.bin
!challenges/*.cf32

# Editors and the operating system
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# The final exercise. It is not part of the repository the students clone:
# the answer key is in there, the two images are 60 MB each and over GitHub's
# limit, and src/ vendors the whole of cFS and CryptoLib. It travels on the
# USB stick. Decision of 9 November 2026.
pwncube/
# And any package made from it. A zip or tarball of that directory carries the
# answer key inside, and the directory rule above does not cover a file. One
# was found untracked in the working tree on 9 November 2026, 152 MB, with
# VULNERABILITIES.md in it.
pwncube*.zip
pwncube*.tgz
pwncube*.tar
pwncube*.tar.gz
